{"study_accession":"PRJNA1185283","secondary_study_accession":"SRP544755","title":"Whole blood RNA sequencing of African American kidney transplant recipients from VericiDx cohort","description":"The VericiDx cohort is an ongoing clinical trial (241 patients (32.0% self-reported AA) enrolled as of 06/30/2023) with a focus on predicting early acute rejection and renal fibrosis post-transplantation (ClinicalTrials.gov: NCT04727788). Overall design: Pretransplant RNA sequencing profiles (101 PE reads) were generated on pretransplant blood, with a subset of 77 recipients. The RNA data in these 77 AA recipients was combined with two cohorts to identify the meta-gene signatures associated with the LILRB3-4SNPs. The LILRB3-4SNPs was correlated with early eGFR values (within two years) in meta-analysis with other three cohorts. However, the relatively short follow-up duration for many patients in this cohort limited the association analysis for graft failure.","pubmed":"40065170","geo_series":"","n_samples":13,"study_labels":[{"level":"study","event_code":"ORGAN_TRANSPLANT","certainty":"confirmed","delta_days":-60.0,"delta_bucket":"B_FAR","time_precision":"approx","stage":"teacher","confidence":1.0,"evidence":"Whole blood RNA sequencing of African American kidney transplant recipients from VericiDx cohort","model_version":"teacher:mlx:mlx-community/Qwen2.5-14B-Instruct-4bit"}],"samples":[{"sample_accession":"SAMN44700630","study_accession":"PRJNA1185283","blood_class":"whole_blood","class_from":"sample","title":"baselineLILR095","description":"baselineLILR095","sex":"female","geo_sample":"GSM8626749","access":"open","dbgap":"","n_runs":1,"first_public":"2025-01-29","attributes":[["source_name","Whole blood"],["tissue","Whole blood"],["genotype","No risk allele"],["sex","female"],["ethnicity","Not Hispanic or Latino"],["self-reported race","African American"],["geo_loc_name","missing"],["collection_date","missing"]],"runs":[{"run_accession":"SRR31319264","experiment_accessio